  "timing_boundaries": {
    "allocation_full_process": "Fresh worker for each arm. Initialization and complete100-point warm traversal outside timer. SYSTEM_CLOCK surrounds one100-point RUN, including point copy, scale/coupling update, Fortran numerator and kinematics, reduction, scalar masters, stability/actual rescue, status counting and final timed answer/accuracy/status copies. Formatting/serialization and process start/stop outside. One worker exits0 before next.",
    "native_request_screen": "One complete private MpState::evaluate for each1392 ordered requests: recover113bit ASCII, widen256bit, reset/bind tensor, rebuild reduction inputs, reduction/scalar masters, format8ASCII fields. Reused independent state/cache perpolicy. Request objects/result-vector capacity prepared outside; returned output-buffer allocation/push inside. Serialization and returned-buffer release outside. Excludes MadLoop Fortran numerator/kinematics, stability controller, and public manager IPC. No cost subtraction.",
    "older_callback": "Sum1392 per-record intervals around shared dispatch plus ordered tensor evaluate/expansion methods writing preallocated outputs. Coefficient binding, parsing, cloning, views/output allocation, comparisons, formatting/serialization outside. No amplitude/cut/geometry/master construction or calls. No-op timing retained, not subtracted.",
    "older_Fortran": "Fresh uninstrumented standalone check perarm/repetition; initialization/warm traversal outside timer, separate full-output evidence pass before timing. SYSTEM_CLOCK includes all100 scale/coupling updates and full SLOOPMATRIX_THRES amplitude calls with real rescues and status histogram, excludes serialization. Consequently exact row evidence is from the untimed pass, unlike allocation worker final timed traversal."
  },
  "interpretation_limits": [
    "3.15% whole-process allocation,9.24% pure tensor callback and3.19% Ninja6 Fortran prototype are separate comparisons and cannot be added or treated as the same workload.",
    "Allocation measured existing NinjaRS original tensor vs allocation tensor, not original MadLoop with Ninja.",
    "Native screen rejects promotion under the declared upperCI<1 rule; confidence intervals cross1, so no statistically demonstrated improvement or slowdown.",
    "None of these studies closes the final eight-process original-Ninja5% acceptance gate.",
    "Older Fortran package honestly remained isolated/not acceptance eligible at capture; later source promotion must use its separate production proof."
  ],
